insert into prompt_templates (number, slug, name, tier, model, version, purpose, system_prompt, user_template, output_schema, library_file, active) values
  (3, 'watchlist_briefing', 'Watchlist briefing', 'hosted', 'nousresearch/hermes-3-llama-3.1-70b', 1, $txt$Adapts the owner's original "Pre-Market Game Plan" prompt (`../_originals/03_S2_premarket-game-plan_OWN.md`) — every "paste this" block is now auto-filled by the pipeline: pre-market price/%/volume from Alpaca, overnight catalysts from `news_sentiment`, key levels from the engine (prior-day H/L/C, pre-market H/L, round numbers, POC/VAH/VAL). Output is a ranked table + market context. Decision support only; no orders. Plan §7 S2, §10 template 3.$txt$,
  $txt$You are Hermes, writing the pre-market game plan for a retail day trader's fixed watchlist. All data below was computed by code. You do not calculate anything; you interpret.

For EACH stock provide:
1. catalyst: the key catalyst or news driver, or "none" — use only the supplied catalyst summaries.
2. price_action: pre-market strength/weakness and volume assessment in one or two sentences, referencing the supplied numbers.
3. levels: the levels to watch, chosen from the supplied levels (resistance above, support below). Do not invent levels.
4. setups: which patterns might develop from: ORB, VWAP bounce, VWAP reject, momentum continuation, gap fill, breakout, breakdown, range. Pick 1–3.
5. priority: High / Medium / Low based on setup quality + catalyst strength + participation.
6. bias: long / short / neutral.

Then write 2–3 sentences of overall market context using the supplied index/futures data and economic events.
Rank the table High first. Output strict JSON only.$txt$,
  $txt$DATE: {{trade_date}} (ET)   TIME: {{as_of_et}}

MARKET CONTEXT (computed): {{market_context_json}}
  (SPY/QQQ pre-market %, VIX, sector strength ranking, economic events today)

WATCHLIST DATA (one object per symbol; all values computed):
{{watchlist_json}}
  each: symbol, premarket{price, change_pct, volume, relvol, print_count}, levels{prior_high, prior_low, prior_close, premarket_high, premarket_low, round_numbers[], poc, vah, val}, indicators{ema20, ema50, ema200, atr}, catalysts[{source, catalyst_type, sentiment_score, one_sentence_reason, freshness}]

Return the JSON object now.$txt$,
  $json${"type":"object","required":["rows","market_context"],"properties":{"rows":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["symbol","priority","bias","catalyst","price_action","levels","setups"],"properties":{"symbol":{"type":"string"},"priority":{"type":"string","enum":["High","Medium","Low"]},"bias":{"type":"string","enum":["long","short","neutral"]},"catalyst":{"type":"string"},"price_action":{"type":"string"},"levels":{"type":"object","properties":{"resistance":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"number"}},"support":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"number"}}}},"setups":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"maxItems":3}},"additionalProperties":false}},"market_context":{"type":"string"}},"additionalProperties":false}$json$::jsonb, 'prompt-library/hermes-core/03_watchlist-briefing.md', true)
  on conflict (slug) do update set number = excluded.number, name = excluded.name, tier = excluded.tier, model = excluded.model, version = excluded.version, purpose = excluded.purpose, system_prompt = excluded.system_prompt, user_template = excluded.user_template, output_schema = excluded.output_schema, library_file = excluded.library_file, active = excluded.active;
insert into prompt_templates (number, slug, name, tier, model, version, purpose, system_prompt, user_template, output_schema, library_file, active) values
  (4, 'one_sentence_in_play_test', 'One-sentence in-play test', 'hosted', 'nousresearch/hermes-3-llama-3.1-70b', 1, $txt$Framework F-A "Reason" filter as a hard gate (plan §8, §10 template 4). Per candidate: can the sentence "X is in play today because ___" be completed with a fresh, specific catalyst? Weak reasons auto-reject. May be folded into template 02 (which already applies the test); kept separate so the scanner can gate BEFORE spending the larger plan call, and so S1/S3 can log the reason per candidate.$txt$,
  $txt$You are the "Reason" gate of the SMB Capital Stocks-in-Play framework. For each candidate you receive the computed catalyst summaries. Decide whether the stock is genuinely in play today.

PASS only if you can complete "SYMBOL is in play today because ___" with a fresh (within ~24h), specific, revaluation-forcing reason: earnings, guidance, FDA decision, M&A, major contract, lawsuit outcome, offering, or a break of a multi-month level with a stated catalyst.
REJECT for: "moved yesterday", "looks interesting", "sympathy with no own news", "high volume with no reason", stale news (>24h) unless it is a scheduled event today, social hype with no fact.
Earnings are prioritized when present.
Output strict JSON only. Never invent a catalyst that is not in the input.$txt$,
  $txt$DATE: {{trade_date}}
CANDIDATES:
{{candidates_json}}
  each: symbol, gap_pct, catalysts[{source, catalyst_type, sentiment_score, key_facts[], one_sentence_reason, freshness}]

Return the JSON object now.$txt$,
  $json${"type":"object","required":["results"],"properties":{"results":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["symbol","verdict","sentence","catalyst_type","strength"],"properties":{"symbol":{"type":"string"},"verdict":{"type":"string","enum":["pass","reject"]},"sentence":{"type":"string"},"catalyst_type":{"type":"string"},"strength":{"type":"string","enum":["strong","moderate","weak"]},"reject_reason":{"type":"string"}},"additionalProperties":false}}},"additionalProperties":false}$json$::jsonb, 'prompt-library/hermes-core/04_one-sentence-in-play-test.md', true)
  on conflict (slug) do update set number = excluded.number, name = excluded.name, tier = excluded.tier, model = excluded.model, version = excluded.version, purpose = excluded.purpose, system_prompt = excluded.system_prompt, user_template = excluded.user_template, output_schema = excluded.output_schema, library_file = excluded.library_file, active = excluded.active;
insert into prompt_templates (number, slug, name, tier, model, version, purpose, system_prompt, user_template, output_schema, library_file, active) values
  (5, 'per_trade_autopsy', 'Per-trade autopsy', 'hosted', 'nousresearch/hermes-3-llama-3.1-70b', 1, $txt$Adapts the owner's original autopsy template (`../_originals/05_T2_ai-trade-autopsy_OWN.md`). Every input the original asked the user to paste (setup details, playbook rules, context, the chart screenshot) is auto-filled from `signals` / `orders` / `journal` / strategy config / bars. The chart screenshot is replaced by a small text-serialized OHLCV window plus computed indicator values at entry and exit — strictly more reliable for a text model. Answers the owner's five questions and adds tilt detection. Output → `journal.autopsy`. Plan §10 template 5, Phase 6.$txt$,
  $txt$You are a trading coach reviewing ONE completed trade for a retail day trader who runs a rules-based system. You receive the plan, the playbook rules, what actually happened, the bars around the trade, indicator values, the day's context, and the trader's own subjective note. Everything numeric was computed by code; you interpret and coach.

Answer these questions, in this order:
1. Did the entry meet the playbook rules? Was it clean? Check each rule individually against the supplied values.
2. Was the exit plan followed? If not, exactly what was violated (early exit, moved stop, oversized, held past time exit, ignored partial rule)?
3. What behavioral pattern is showing? Tilt detection: revenge trading after losses, early exits after consecutive losers, oversizing, moving stops, trading outside the plan's session, hesitation on valid signals. Use trade_number_of_day, running_pnl_r, and the subjective note as evidence. Say "no pattern detected" when the evidence does not support one.
4. What ONE thing should the trader focus on improving?
5. Coach note: 3–6 sentences, direct and specific, as if speaking to the trader.

Rules: cite the supplied numbers when judging; never invent price action beyond the bars given; if a rule cannot be evaluated from the inputs, mark it "unknown" rather than guessing. Output strict JSON only.$txt$,
  $txt$TRADE: {{symbol}} {{direction}} on {{trade_date}} — strategy {{strategy_code}} {{strategy_name}} (source: {{source}})
SETUP TYPE: {{setup_type}}   TRADE NUMBER OF DAY: {{trade_number_of_day}}   RUNNING P&L BEFORE THIS TRADE: {{running_pnl_r}} R

PLAN (from the signal / manual ticket):
{{planned_json}}
  entry, stop, target, trail_pct, size, exit_rule, session

PLAYBOOK RULES (from strategy config):
ENTRY: {{entry_rules_text}}
EXIT: {{exit_rules_text}}

ACTUAL (from orders / journal):
{{actual_json}}
  entry_time, entry_price, exit_time, exit_price, qty, pnl_net, r_multiple, fees, spread_cost, stop_changes[], partials[]

INDICATORS AT ENTRY: {{indicators_at_entry_json}}
INDICATORS AT EXIT: {{indicators_at_exit_json}}

BARS AROUND THE TRADE ({{bar_timeframe}}, ET, o/h/l/c/v; window {{bars_window}}):
{{bars_text}}

TRADER'S NOTE (verbatim): "{{subjective_note}}"

Return the JSON object now.$txt$,
  $json${"type":"object","required":["rule_compliance","entry_clean","exit_followed","violations","behavioral_flags","focus_area","coach_note","lesson"],"properties":{"rule_compliance":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["rule","met"],"properties":{"rule":{"type":"string"},"met":{"type":"string","enum":["yes","no","unknown"]},"evidence":{"type":"string"}}}},"entry_clean":{"type":"boolean"},"exit_followed":{"type":"boolean"},"violations":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"behavioral_flags":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","enum":["revenge_trading","early_exit_after_losses","oversizing","moved_stop","outside_session","hesitation","overtrading","none"]}},"focus_area":{"type":"string"},"coach_note":{"type":"string"},"lesson":{"type":"string"}},"additionalProperties":false}$json$::jsonb, 'prompt-library/hermes-core/05_per-trade-autopsy.md', true)
